                        "sense_id": "8c5d4887-70a0-3899-b3c8-1349a0282303",
                        "entry_id": "1bcfbbb0-55bf-3e72-bc78-b5c7390f8ee7",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Diagramme représentant l’évolution de l’apparence du ciel visible en un point donné en fonction du temps."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "784a9eab-1c28-4678-b877-c44ffe603450",
                                "sense_id": "8c5d4887-70a0-3899-b3c8-1349a0282303",
                                "text": "Autour de minuit, on observe un puit assez large vers 18:91 UT (00:24 LT) d’environ 12% de la valeur maximum. Afin de détailler cette particularité, nous traçons un kéogramme (figure 4.20). Un kéogramme est construit à partir de la colonne centrale de chaque image de la vidéo"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "e189aad2-5781-4e4d-8afc-e129e165282c",
                        "source_entry_id": "1bcfbbb0-55bf-3e72-bc78-b5c7390f8ee7",
                        "source_sense_id": "8c5d4887-70a0-3899-b3c8-1349a0282303",
                        "target_lang_word": "keogram",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "keogram",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "0235357e-d1e6-3f11-a79a-490e22ca2d00",
                                        "entry_id": "446b7390-7ea2-350e-a8a4-c3b058735772",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A photographic method of capturing aurorae."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8d9c9119-87c6-42b6-a6a2-e01b1459871f",
                                                "sense_id": "0235357e-d1e6-3f11-a79a-490e22ca2d00",
                                                "text": "Various types of data formats can be obtained starting with the digitized data. One currently being used in combination with magnetospheric studies is the \"keogram\" picture⁽⁴⁾. This technique combines each intensity versus zenith angle scan on a horizontal time axis."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "bf2de66f-dff0-43f5-842e-9dcb912c6436",
                                                "sense_id": "0235357e-d1e6-3f11-a79a-490e22ca2d00",
                                                "text": "A diagram of the latitudinal variations with time is sometimes called a keogram. Neither scanning photometers nor cameras are sufficiently sensitive to record the most rapid fluctuations in the auroral emissions, but TV techniques, both monochrome and color, are more sensitive and have been applied very successfully to dynamic auroral photography in recent years. In addition to their scientific value, some of these auroral \"videos\" are possessed of no little esthetic interest (particularly if they are set to music). Figure 6.9 shows an example of a keogram composed from TV data."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "db5d5c55-8004-4389-bfac-f31415ee0b0d",
                                                "sense_id": "0235357e-d1e6-3f11-a79a-490e22ca2d00",
                                                "text": "A ewogram is similar to a keogram except that the vertical axis is magnetic longitude instead of magnetic latitude for a keogram."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "72080767-4711-488c-b2c4-b8a043e60f30",
                                                "sense_id": "0235357e-d1e6-3f11-a79a-490e22ca2d00",
                                                "text": "In this paper we argue that the photometric keogram technique is more reliable and more accurate than all-sky cameras for cusp monitoring, and gives minute-by-minute time resolution not possible with satellite data."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "99285bee-4b17-4fe3-88d0-21bddbc8dee6",
                                                "sense_id": "0235357e-d1e6-3f11-a79a-490e22ca2d00",
                                                "text": "Observation and classification results from the night of 22–23 October 2017. The middle panel shows a keogram, which is a time series of the north-south cross-section of the all-sky image, and the bottom panel is the classification result for the same period."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
